A brands. The company sells its products through wholesale channels, including national and regional sporting goods chains, independent and specialty retailers, department store chains, mono-branded Under Armour retail stores, institutional athletic departments, and leagues and teams, as well as independent distributors; and directly to consumers through its own brand and factory house retail stores and e-commerce websites. It operates in the United States, Canada, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, the Asia-Pacific, and Latin America. The company was incorporated in 1996 and is headquartered in Baltimore, Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin A. Plank | Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $801K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 10%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Under Armour, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.3B market cap on $5.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +0% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 48%.","The company is burning through $162M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -9.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 9.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (43.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 76% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7557877668678497},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 65/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Under Armour (UAA) Cuts Its Loss As Sales Weaken, Is It Still Undervalued?","sour